<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Adding and subtracting surds</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Simplify the following, giving your answer in the form \( a\sqrt{b} \), where \(b\) has no square factors:</p>
<p>
\[ {@A@}\sqrt{ {@m1@} } \;{@signchar@}\; {@Bmag@}\sqrt{ {@m2@} } \]
</p>
<p>
\( a = \) [[input:ans1]] ; \( \sqrt{b} \), \( b = \) [[input:ans2]]
</p>
<p>[[validation:ans1]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<p></p><p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<![CDATA[ 
<p>First simplify each surd separately, by finding the largest perfect-square factor of each number under the root:</p>
<p>
\[ \sqrt{ {@m1@} } = \sqrt{ {@(a1^2)@} \times {@p@} } = {@a1@}\sqrt{ {@p@} } \]
</p>
<p>
\[ \sqrt{ {@m2@} } = \sqrt{ {@(a2^2)@} \times {@p@} } = {@a2@}\sqrt{ {@p@} } \]
</p>
<p>Substitute these back into the original expression:</p>
<p>
\[
{@A@}\sqrt{ {@m1@} } \;{@signchar@}\; {@Bmag@}\sqrt{ {@m2@} }
= {@A@}\times {@a1@}\sqrt{ {@p@} } \;{@signchar@}\; {@Bmag@}\times {@a2@}\sqrt{ {@p@} }
= {@(A*a1)@}\sqrt{ {@p@} } \;{@signchar@}\; {@(Bmag*a2)@}\sqrt{ {@p@} }
\]
</p>
<p>Both terms now have the same surd part, \( \sqrt{ {@p@} } \), so they are &ldquo;like surds&rdquo; and their coefficients can be combined:</p>
<p>
\[ = {@coeff@}\sqrt{ {@p@} } \]
</p>
 ]]]]><![CDATA[>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
